HEADLINE: Harbour Street Library Reopens After Nine-Week Renovation

- The library reopened on Monday after nine weeks of renovation work.
- The roof was replaced, and the children's section moved from the basement to the ground floor.
- The reading room now has 60 seats, up from 38, plus a quiet area with power sockets.
- A free workshop room is available for local groups, with a knitting circle and a teen coding club already booked.
- Opening hours have changed, with later closing on Tuesdays and Thursdays and earlier opening on Saturdays.

